/* ==========================================================================
   CAMERA LAB v1 — Cameras Decoded game module
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The Virtual Mirrorless Camera Lab: live viewfinder with real exposure
   physics (EV brightness, aperture DoF, shutter motion blur, ISO grain,
   blinkies, live histogram), a tactile dial, white balance control, six
   progressive scenarios (Studio → Bright Beach → Wildlife → Dim Wedding →
   Indoor Arena → Blue Hour Neon), graded instructor briefs with
   bronze/silver/gold tiers, "why" physics diagnostics, and a session-only
   Field Pocketbook.

   Ported from the standalone simulator (single-file HTML export). Adaptations
   for the arcade contract:
     - All UI mounts inside the `stage` element; every CSS class/ID is
       namespaced under `.cl-` / `.cl-root` (zero collisions with site CSS).
     - Exposure is applied with a cheap overlay rect, NOT per-frame
       ctx.filter brightness; the DoF blur is pre-rendered once per aperture
       change into an offscreen layer (bokeh cache), never per frame.
     - ISO grain uses CDGames.fx.grainTiles() (pre-rendered tiles, cycled).
     - rAF loop is pausable/resumable; destroy() tears everything down.
     - Shutter uses CDGames.shutterClick(); haptics use CDGames.fx.tap().
     - Scoring: getSnapshot() returns the player's BEST brief result (0-100).
       Solving a brief advances api.hud(); solving all 12 briefs ends the
       session via api.finish(). Pocketbook stays in-memory (session-only).
     - Daily mode: init(stage, {daily:true}, api) locks the lab to a single
       brief picked deterministically from the 12-brief pool by local
       day-of-year (same convention as the daily drill), hides the scenario
       and tier pickers behind a "Today's brief" banner, and finishes after
       that one brief is solved. All physics, grading, and scoring unchanged.
   ========================================================================== */
